<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>apark_b1</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author><name>CellularSheaves.jl</name><email>adamkadosh@gmail.com</email></author>
  <description>
    Unitree B1, standing. Trunk, hips, thighs and calves are Unitree's own meshes
    from unitree_ros/robots/b1_description, placed by the forward kinematics of
    b1.urdf at a symmetric stance so the feet rest on the ground plane. The legs
    are visual only: the B1 is driven as a unicycle because it accepts the same
    Twist a Jackal does, and gait is out of scope for this demo, so four hidden
    contact bodies under the trunk carry the same DiffDrive plugin, the same
    topics and the same odometry the Jackal publishes.
  </description>
</model>
